      "content": "<h3>Best practices</h3>\n<p>Keep the natural order simple and correct.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Implement <code>Comparable</code> only when one order is clearly \"the\" order (name, id, date).</li>\n<li>Always use <code>Integer.compare</code> / <code>Double.compare</code>, never subtraction.</li>\n<li>Keep <code>compareTo</code> consistent with <code>equals</code> and <code>hashCode</code>.</li>\n<li>Compare the same fields in <code>equals</code> and <code>compareTo</code>; add a tie-breaker field if needed.</li>\n<li>Use <code>Comparator</code> for any extra orders and for classes you cannot modify.</li>\n<li>Do not use mutable fields in <code>compareTo</code> for objects stored in a TreeSet or TreeMap.</li>\n</ul>"
